.TH TXT2IMG 1 "May 2026" "txt2img" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
txt2img \- Render ANSI-styled text into high-quality images

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B txt2img
.RB [ \-W
.IR width ]
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.RB [ FILE ]
.br
.B cat
.I FILE
|
.B txt2img
.B \-W
.I width
.RB [ OPTIONS ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B txt2img
is a robust command-line utility designed to render text, including text containing ANSI escape sequences (SGR), into visually appealing images. It is particularly useful for capturing terminal output, code snippets, or any text that benefits from colorization and styling.
.PP
Key features include:
.IP \(bu 3
Full support for 8, 16, and 24-bit (TrueColor) ANSI colors.
.IP \(bu 3
Support for \fBbold\fR and \fIitalic\fR text styles.
.IP \(bu 3
Automatic word wrapping based on a specified pixel width.
.IP \(bu 3
Multi-page output when a maximum height is specified.
.IP \(bu 3
Customizable fonts, sizes, padding, and colors.
.PP
If \fIFILE\fR is provided, \fBtxt2img\fR reads from it. If \fIFILE\fR is omitted or is '\-', it reads from standard input.

.SH OPTIONS
.SS "General Options"
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Display a comprehensive help message and exit.
.TP
.BI \-t\ " text"\fR, \fB\-\-text=\fR"\fItext\fR"
Process the provided string directly instead of reading from a file or stdin. Use '\\n' to represent literal newlines within the string.

.SS "Image Dimensions"
.TP
.BI \-W\ " pixels"\fR, \fB\-\-width=\fR"\fIpixels\fR"
(\fBRequired\fR) Set the total width of the generated image in pixels. Text will be wrapped to fit within this width minus padding.
.TP
.BI \-H\ " pixels"\fR, \fB\-\-height=\fR"\fIpixels\fR"
Set a maximum height for the image. If the rendered text exceeds this height, \fBtxt2img\fR will split the content across multiple image files.
.TP
.B \-T\fR, \fB\-\-trim\-height
When used with \fB\-\-height\fR, this flag ensures the last image (or the only image) is trimmed to the height of the actual content rather than using the full specified height.

.SS "Rendering Control"
.TP
.B \-r\fR, \fB\-\-raw
Disable ANSI escape sequence parsing. Text will be rendered literally, and control characters will likely appear as placeholders or be ignored depending on the font.

.SS "Output Selection"
.TP
.BI \-n\ " name"\fR, \fB\-\-file\-name=\fR"\fIname\fR"
Specify the base name for the output image(s). Defaults to \fBoutput.png\fR. For multi-page output, files are named \fIname_1.png\fR, \fIname_2.png\fR, etc.
.TP
.BI \-o\ " dir"\fR, \fB\-\-output\-directory=\fR"\fIdir\fR"
Specify the directory where the output images will be saved. Defaults to the current working directory.

.SS "Styling and Formatting"
.TP
.BI \-\-fg\fR "\fI color\fR"
Set the default foreground (text) color. Accepts hex codes like "#RRGGBB" or "RRGGBB". Defaults to a dark gray (#222222).
.TP
.BI \-\-bg\fR "\fI color\fR"
Set the background color of the image. Accepts hex codes. Defaults to a light cream (#f6efdf).
.TP
.BI \-\-font\fR "\fI path\fR"
Provide the absolute or relative path to a TrueType (.ttf) or OpenType (.otf) font file to use for rendering. If not provided, \fBtxt2img\fR attempts to find a suitable monospace font on the system.
.TP
.BI \-\-font\-size\fR "\fI pixels\fR"
Set the font size in pixels. Defaults to 20.
.TP
.BI \-\-padding\fR "\fI pixels\fR"
Set the amount of space between the text and the edge of the image. Defaults to 20 pixels.
.TP
.BI \-\-tabsize\fR "\fI width\fR"
Specify the number of spaces to use for tab characters. Defaults to 4.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B Basic usage with a file:
.RS 4
txt2img -W 800 notes.txt
.RE
.PP
.B Using stdin and custom output:
.RS 4
cat log.ansi | txt2img -W 1200 -n system_log.png -o ~/Pictures
.RE
.PP
.B Rendering direct text with styling:
.RS 4
txt2img -W 500 --fg "#00FF00" --bg "000000" -t "SUCCESS: Operation Complete\nTime: 45ms"
.RE
.PP
.B Creating a multi-page document:
.RS 4
txt2img -W 1000 -H 1500 -T -n manual long_document.txt
.RE
.PP
.B Piping from a command with colors:
.RS 4
ls -la --color=always | txt2img -W 900 --font "/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSansMono.ttf"
.RE

